{"id": "EUVD-2026-86636", "enisaUuid": "c88f0ea7-0b0b-3897-a1ef-b178b46b0bcb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ethernet: cortina: Fix budget accounting\n\nThe gmac_rx() function returns the remaining NAPI budget, but its\ncaller treats the return value as the number of packets received. An\nidle poll therefore reports a full budget and remains scheduled.\n\nReturn the number of received packets instead. Preserve the existing\nfree queue refill accounting by adding that count directly; continuing\nto subtract it from the budget would invert the refill behavior.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3deb54d9507c2d7f05efd896142095eef5b7d85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6e5732b90d0fc25fd3d9961ff61e660297d7608", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa339ac334d4e51f43af9d2901e6faf11ffd981e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ca84049c6428c665ef7c903a32a99ed0f1e01e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/631c47e2e1154f2741c555b91df1b8cb99294c6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ef8eaef5806c84db2334111d6f299c246a592bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94e06e12a376710587cfeea481b65e7c49747003", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0de06d0da78a3db53de65dfd7452cc6d111f703"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f9c6-x48g-gfm4", "CVE-2026-97982"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a72df47-a6fa-381e-9407-ea54f37a47a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "0e133f11-57a9-39f0-b8b1-b3ea106cf5c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4d5ae32f5e1e13f7f36d6439ec3257993b9f5b88 <631c47e2e1154f2741c555b91df1b8cb99294c6a"}, {"id": "26d99461-2ce9-369a-b71c-a4837b6062ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4d5ae32f5e1e13f7f36d6439ec3257993b9f5b88 <0ef8eaef5806c84db2334111d